From d4edb89fa82281ab7655508c6f822a6656b5b9ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:15:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(sim): the span floor's tilt cap is closed at 90 degrees

#1306's span floor read the interval bound for any span with an A/B
letter at exactly +-90, because the cap that lets the samples bound the
span was strict. A blade-lying swarf link (B +90 -> -90) then pinned its
horizontal end's -R floor onto the B 45 pose's footprint, where the band
stands about 34 mm over the tip: 18 false SweepHits in the release
lane's full-band swarf tests.

On the closed cap cos A and cos B stay >= 0 along the lerp and
ln cos A + ln cos B is concave, so cos(tilt) is least at an end, by
continuity also at an end where it is 0: the samples still bound the
span. Letters past 90 keep the interval floor.

Pinned by verify::sweep::tests::a_swing_through_vertical_reads_no_floor_from_its_horizontal_ends
and the closed-cap brute lerp in tilt_span's cap test; both fail on the
strict cap.

Fixes #1404

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
